  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Dadasaheb Jalindar Kudande vs State Of Maharashtra on 6 July, 2022 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 908-Aba1815-22.Doc Santos Santosh Subhash In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Kulkarni Digitally signed by Santosh Subhash Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Kulkarni Date: 2022.07.08 10:24:08 +0530 Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1815 Of 2022 Dadasaheb Jalindar Kudande ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. Ganesh Bhujbal, for the Applicant. Mrs. P. N. Dabholkar, App for the State Coram: N. J. Jamadar, J. Dated : 6th July, 2022 Order: 2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.149 of 2022, registered with Yawat Police Station, District Pune, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 and 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Section 26(2)(1), 26(2) and 27(2) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.149 of 2022, registered with Yawat Police Station, District Pune, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 and 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Section 26(2)(1), 26(2) and 27(2) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. Smt. Kranti Baravkar, the Food Safety Officer, lodged a report with the allegations that a tempo of Eicher make was intercepted. On search, 16,200 packets of scented tobacco/ paan-masala and other Dadasaheb Jalindar Kudande vs State Of Maharashtra on 6 July, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/41744507/ 1 contraband articles were found. 908-ABA1815-22.DOC Co-accused Yasin Khan, who was on the wheel of the said vehicle, came to be apprehended. The incriminating articles were seized. It transpired that the said contraband articles were to be delivered to the applicant. Hence, the first informant lodged report against the person, who was found transporting, the person who had dispatched the said contraband articles, and the applicant to whom they were to be delivered. 4. The learned Counsel for the applicant submitted that the the applicant has no role whatsoever in the transportation of the contraband articles. The provisions contained in Section 328 of the Penal Code have been unjustifiably invoked.",
